            <ArticleTitle>Extensive pneumatization of the temporal bone and articular eminence: an incidental finding in a patient with facial pain. Case report and review of literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>211-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 53-year-old Caucasian female presented to the Oral Medicine Department at the hospital of the University of Pennsylvania for consultation regarding facial pain. A panoramic radiograph revealed multilocular radiolucencies in the right articular eminence. A CT scan was then performed, and the radiolucencies were determined to be pneumatization of the articular eminence.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
